messages:
Mia: Quick sync — we need a decision on rerank response shape vs console model-priority UX before next week's rollout. Some clients require a single scalar score, others want per-feature breakdown (logits, position bias, language-features). Can we support both without exploding quotas/console complexity?

Devon: +1, we should support two explicit modes: 'compact' (scalar only) and 'detailed' (breakdown array). Add a request field `score_mode` and a response envelope `scores.mode`. Console shows tenant preference. :thinking:

Sourav: Important: billing/quota must be invariant. Whether breakdown or scalar, tenant should be charged the same unit (we already charge per candidate_score_unit). If detailed adds size, still count as 1 candidate. Otherwise ops will get angry.

Chris: Model selection note — if we let tenants pick a preferred model in Console, routing must treat that as a soft affinity. We need fallback rules when preferred model is saturated (auto-fallback to cheaper/compatible variant). Recommend header `X-Model-Preference` with `weight` in routing table.

Ana: Telemetry ask: dashboard needs per-model sample %, per-score-mode split, P50/P95 latency, and a sample of breakdowns (anonymized). Also telemetry for position-dropoff so product can tune topK. UI: toggle to preview 'compact' vs 'detailed' on live requests.

Mia: Sounds good. Proposed rollout: default to 'compact' for all tenants, add 'detailed' behind a tenant flag + canary. Console exposes two toggles: Preferred model (soft) and Score mode (compact/detailed). Provide a one-click migration helper that converts detailed -> compact by applying a configured aggregation (e.g., weighted sum).

Devon: Example payloads for clarity:
```json
// compact response
{
  "scores": {"mode":"compact","values":[0.83,0.72,0.12]}
}
// detailed response
{
  "scores": {
    "mode":"detailed",
    "values":[
      {"total":0.83,"components":{"logit":1.1,"position_penalty":-0.3}},
      {"total":0.72,"components":{"logit":0.95,"position_penalty":-0.23}}
    ]
  }
}
```
Devon: If we keep billing unchanged, this won't be a hard sell. We'll add a schema version field so clients can opt-in.

Sourav: Edge case: variable topK per-request. If client requests topK=50, we still count 50 candidate units. Dashboard should show candidate unit distribution not just request count.

Chris: Console UX: show current routing hits and indicate when preferred model is degraded (red/yellow). Provide an automatic fallback policy that can be selected: FAILFAST | SOFT_FALLBACK | FORCE_ALT. Default SOFT_FALLBACK.

Ana: For telemetry panels I also want a small sampled table of raw detailed scores (PII-safe) so ML can surface drift/regression. Sampling rate per-tenant configurable in Console.

Mia: OK action items: Devon — draft API PR for `score_mode` + schema version; Sourav — ensure billing invariants in quota service; Chris — design fallback enum + routing header; Ana — telemetry panels and sampling controls; I'll wire Console toggles and canary flow.

console-bot: Created tracking ticket RW-PLAT-1342 and canary dashboard: https://dash.internal/rw/1342 (auto-summary).

Devon: I'll throw up a short prototyping PR with tests by EOD. :thumbsup:

Sourav: +1 on the plan, will reserve a quick quota-run to validate.

Ana: Thanks — I'll draft dashboard mocks and share in #product tomorrow.

Mia: Great. If anyone wants to add edge cases (compression, size limits for detailed comps), ping me.

Chris: One more note — let's document fallback semantics in the Console help tooltip so customers know when their preferred model might not be used.

Mia: Good call. I'll add that to the rollout checklist.
